<!--
    looptest, top tests without a guard to drop: more loops whose first top
    test is proven, and loops whose test at the top is the same program
    whatever their first test is.

    Issue: kuna-looptest3 (decbench O2: rotated loops printed do-while because
    their entry test was not recognised, or their test at the bottom recomputes
    the value a carried variable already holds).  Stage P8 (goto-quality), P0
    assertion `option looptest binary|proven|assume` (default `proven`).

    The bytes are .text of authored C built by gcc 11.4 -O2 -fno-inline
    -fcf-protection=none -fno-tree-vectorize (ten_o0 at -O0), linked at
    0x100000 with the helpers poll_busy, touch and release:
      spin        while (poll_busy()) ;   (an empty body)
      skip_spaces do c = *s++; while (c == ' '); return c;
                  (control: the test reads a body value)
      each_index  for (i = 0; i < n; i++) touch(&i);   (i lives in the frame
                  because its address is taken; the function is optimized)
      ten_o0      i = 0; do { touch(&i); i++; } while (i < 10);   at -O0
                  (control: an unoptimized function's frame counter)
      free_args   if (a->list && a->num < a->nalloc) for (i = 0; i < a->num;
                  i++) ...   (the guard reuses the load of a->num in the
                  `&&` block before it)
      reset_free  a->nalloc = 0; for (i = 0; i < a->num; i++) ...   (gcc loads
                  a->num before the store to the field next to it)
      flip_body   for (q = s->body; q != &s->tail; q++) *q ^= 0x5a;   declared
                  with an integer parameter, so both ends are sums s + 8 and
                  s + 0x48
      bump_range  do { *p += 1; p++; } while (p != q);   (control: no proof)
      clear_grid  g->head = 1; then a nested zeroing loop gcc unrolls inside,
                  whose test recomputes the next row pointer

    Pass 1 (default `proven`): spin prints `while (poll_busy()) {}`, which runs
    the same calls as the do-while; each_index, free_args and reset_free drop
    their guards (the guard's load of a->num reads the memory the loop sees);
    flip_body's entry test s + 0x48 != s + 8 folds to true; clear_grid's test
    prints the carried v2 for `&(*v1)[8]`.  skip_spaces, ten_o0 and bump_range
    stay do-whiles.  Pass 2 (`option looptest binary`): every loop is a
    do-while again.
-->
